wrhtml/figures/m6051a3f1.gif","alt":"The figure shows the sampling strategy for an A(H1N1)pdm09 vaccine survey of correctional facilities in the United States during the 2009–10 influenza season. To select the sample, data from the National Commission on Correctional Health Care and the Bureau of Justice Statistics were analyzed. From a sampling frame of 2,949 jails, 1,719 state prisons, and 102 federal prisons, a multistage strategy was used to select 814 jails, 341 state prisons, and 31 federal prisons for the sample.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":620,"renderedHeight":370,"naturalWidth":620,"naturalHeight":370,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 488 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":46713},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/m6051a3f2.gif","alt":"The figure shows the percentage of correctional facilities receiving A(H1N1)pdm09 vaccine, among facilities that provided receipt dates, in the United States during the 2009–10 influenza season. The proportions receiving vaccine by April 2010 were 71% for federal prisons, 55% for state prisons, and 28% for jails.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":605,"renderedHeight":374,"naturalWidth":605,"naturalHeight":374,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 314 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":15331},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_pdf.gif","alt":"Adobe PDF file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"naturalWidth":16,"naturalHeight":16,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":6058},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_wo